      "direction_name": "编辑可靠性与行为控制",
      "week": "2026-W23",
      "title": "CLaRE-ty Amid Chaos: Quantifying Representational Entanglement to Predict Ripple Effects in LLM Editing",
      "title_zh": "混沌中的CLaRE：量化表征纠缠预测大语言模型编辑中的涟漪效应",
      "authors": [
        "Manit Baser",
        "Alperen Yildiz",
        "Dinil Mon Divakaran",
        "M. Gurusamy"
      ],
      "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2603.19297",
      "pdf_url": "http://arxiv.org/pdf/2603.19297",
      "category": "via-citation",
      "published": "",
      "collected": "2026-06-02",
      "abstract": "The static knowledge representations of large language models (LLMs) inevitably become outdated or incorrect over time. While model-editing techniques offer a promising solution by modifying a model's factual associations, they often produce unpredictable ripple effects, which are unintended behavioral changes that propagate even to the hidden space. In this work, we introduce CLaRE, a lightweight representation-level technique to identify where these ripple effects may occur. Unlike prior gradient-based methods, CLaRE quantifies entanglement between facts using forward activations from a single intermediate layer, avoiding costly backward passes. To enable systematic study, we prepare and analyse a corpus of 11,427 facts drawn from three existing datasets. Using CLaRE, we compute large-scale entanglement graphs of this corpus for multiple models, capturing how local edits propagate through representational space. These graphs enable stronger preservation sets for model editing, audit trails, efficient red-teaming, and scalable post-edit evaluation. In comparison to baselines, CLaRE achieves an average of 62.2% improvement in Spearman correlation with ripple effects while being $2.74\\times$ faster, and using $2.85\\times$ less peak GPU memory. Besides, CLaRE requires only a fraction of the storage needed by the baselines to compute and preserve fact representations. Our entanglement graphs and corpus are available at https://github.com/manitbaser/CLaRE.",
      "abstract_zh": "大语言模型的静态知识表征会随时间逐渐过时出错，模型编辑虽可修改事实关联，但常产生不可预测的涟漪效应，即意外行为变化传播到隐空间。本文提出轻量级表征层技术CLaRE，利用单个中间层前向激活量化事实间的纠缠，无需高成本反向传播。本文构建了含11427个事实的语料库，生成多模型的大规模纠缠图，可用于编辑保留集构建、审计等任务。对比基线，CLaRE与涟漪效应的斯皮尔曼相关平均提升62.2%，速度快2.74倍，峰值显存少2.85倍，已开源相关资源。",
      "has_code": true,
      "repo_url": "https://github.com/manitbaser/CLaRE.",
      "repo_stars": 0,
      "hf_upvotes": 0,
      "citation_count": 0,
      "venue": "",
